asn1c 18e56503 runtime: an open type's JER is written through its CHOICE-shaped
struct with the variant member's JER constraints, but read with the bare
type's. For a type written inline in an object set (e.g. BIT STRING (SIZE (24)),
F1AP UEContextSetupResponse) the two differ, so asn1c could not read back its
own JER (and, before 0002, crashed). The decoder now uses the variant member's
constraints. JER serves ksim-codec and the oracle harness only. Row KS-PLAT-D3.

--- a/OPEN_TYPE_jer.c
+++ b/OPEN_TYPE_jer.c
@@ -103,8 +103,13 @@
         (char *)*memb_ptr2
         + elm->type->elements[selected.presence_index - 1].memb_offset;
 
+    /* The variant member's constraints, as CHOICE_encode_jer writes it: the
+     * bare type's are absent for a type written inline in an object set. */
+    const asn_jer_constraints_t *variant_jer =
+        elm->type->elements[selected.presence_index - 1].encoding_constraints.jer_constraints;
     rv = selected.type_descriptor->op->jer_decoder(
-        opt_codec_ctx, selected.type_descriptor, selected.type_descriptor->encoding_constraints.jer_constraints,
+        opt_codec_ctx, selected.type_descriptor,
+        variant_jer ? variant_jer : selected.type_descriptor->encoding_constraints.jer_constraints,
         &inner_value, ptr, size);
     ADVANCE(rv.consumed);
     rv.consumed = 0;
